OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FARCHIVE: The TV Room
OL,7,
OL,8,FThe start of 1975 brought significant
OL,9,Fcuts to BBC services to save money.
OL,10,
OL,11,FAfternoon TV on BBC One went, BBC Two's
OL,12,Fweekend hours were curtailed and both
OL,13,Fnetworks closed by 11.30pm on
OL,14,Fweeknights.
OL,15,
OL,16,FThese were painful cuts which reduced
OL,17,Fchoice for viewers ` in particular
OL,18,Fthose at home in the afternoon
OL,19,Fincluding the housebound.
OL,20,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,131,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13002
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F130A1768740178
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G2/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FOne other cut took effect a few weeks
OL,7,Flater on 20th January 1975.
OL,8,
OL,9,FTrade test transmissions on BBC Two
OL,10,Fwere drastically curtailed.
OL,11,
OL,12,FUp until then, BBC Two transmitters had
OL,13,Fpumped out up to 10 hours of the test
OL,14,Fcard every day `B  generally only
OL,15,Finterrupted for Play School at 11am.
OL,16,
OL,17,FUntil August 1973, the trade test
OL,18,Ftransmissions also included colour
OL,19,Ffilms to provide moving images to
OL,20,Fdemonstrate sets.
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,131,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13003
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F130A1768740178
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G3/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FGoodness knows what the Carbon
OL,7,Ffootprint was, to use the language of
OL,8,Ftoday.
OL,9,
OL,10,FIn January 1975 the axe fell. Generally
OL,11,FBBC Two transmitters were only on the
OL,12,Fair between 10.30am and 11.30am and
OL,13,Ffrom 4pm until shortly after the final
OL,14,Fprogramme of the day.
OL,15,
OL,16,FThe cuts were justified by the need to
OL,17,Fsave both money and fuel.
OL,18,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,131,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13004
SC,0004
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F130A1768740178
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G4/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FAt the time, the corporation would have
OL,7,Fbeen billed for its electricity use
OL,8,Fdirectly in the same way as any other
OL,9,Fbusiness customer.
OL,10,
OL,11,FWhile the draconian power restrictions
OL,12,Fof early 1974 had gone, there were
OL,13,Fstill calls to save fuel.
OL,14,
OL,15,FMost of Britain's electricity came from
OL,16,Fcoal and imported oil ` North Sea oil
OL,17,Fwas still to come on tap.B Cutting the
OL,18,Fuse of power helped to reduce the use
OL,19,Fof oil for electricity generation.
OL,20,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,131,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13005
SC,0005
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F130A1768740178
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G5/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt's hard to argue against the logic of
OL,7,Fthis cut.B Amongst the wider public,
OL,8,Fonly diehard fans of BBC Two's test
OL,9,Fcard music would have been
OL,10,Fdisappointed.
OL,11,
OL,12,FBut there is no doubt that this cut
OL,13,Fcaused significant inconvenience to the
OL,14,Ftrade.
OL,15,
OL,16,FThe lack of a BBC Two signal for much
OL,17,Fof the daytime, made it harder to
OL,18,Finstall sets and aerials.
OL,19,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,131,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13006
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F130A1768740178
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G6/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn editorial in the magazine Television
OL,7,Fin April 1975 highlighted these
OL,8,Fconcerns.
OL,9,
OL,10,FTelevision, originally Practical
OL,11,FTelevision, was a useful magazine with
OL,12,Fgood advice for service engineers and
OL,13,FDX enthusiasts.
OL,14,
OL,15,FThe basic concerns were justified but I
OL,16,Fcannot help but think the writer went
OL,17,Fslightly over the score.
OL,18,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,131,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13007
SC,0007
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F130A1768740178
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G7/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FFirst of all ` would the loss of the
OL,7,FBBC Two test card really cause massive
OL,8,Fproblems and lead to more badly
OL,9,Fadjusted sets?
OL,10,
OL,11,FFundamental adjustments to set up
OL,12,Ftelevisions ` like convergence checks
OL,13,Fand balancing the colour guns ` should
OL,14,Fhave been done in the workshop, not a
OL,15,Fhome. Many of these checks should have
OL,16,Fbeen done with pattern generators.
OL,17,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,131,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13008
SC,0008
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F130A1768740178
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G8/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen a set was installed in the
OL,7,Fviewer's home, it should only have been
OL,8,Fnecessary to tune it in and adjust the
OL,9,Fnormal controls like the brightness and
OL,10,Fcontrast.
OL,11,
OL,12,FThe test card was basically diagnostic
OL,13,F` it showed up faults and allowed for
OL,14,Fadjustments.
OL,15,
OL,16,FThe loss of the test card on BBC Two
OL,17,Fwas, of course, partly balanced out by
OL,18,Fits increased use on BBC One in the
OL,19,Fafternoon after the programme cuts.
OL,20,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,131,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13009
SC,0009
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F130A1768740178
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G9/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe suggestion thatB there would often
OL,7,Fbe no colour signal to show the viewer
OL,8,Fseems a strange one.
OL,9,
OL,10,FBy 1975, roughly half ofB BBC Schools
OL,11,Fprogrammes were in colour ` including
OL,12,Fall new ones.B  ITV meanwhile ran a
OL,13,Ffull schedule from noon ` nothing was
OL,14,Fin black and white except for the odd
OL,15,Ffilm.
OL,16,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,131,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13010
SC,0010
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F130A1768740178
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                G10/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FA point about the colour quality of
OL,7,Fsome programmes is highly dubious.
OL,8,FSchools and daytime programmes operated
OL,9,Fto the same technical standards as the
OL,10,Frest of the schedule.
OL,11,
OL,12,FWhile the lack of any signal was
OL,13,Fcertainly inconvenient, UHF aerials
OL,14,Fgenerally gave equally good results on
OL,15,Fall channels.
OL,16,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,131,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13011
SC,0011
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F130A1768740178
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                G11/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn aerial properly adjusted for both
OL,7,FBBC One and ITV could be presumed to be
OL,8,Fset up properly for BBC Two. When
OL,9,FChannel 4 started, there was no need
OL,10,Ffor aerial adjustments except in the
OL,11,Ffew instances where Channel 4 was on an
OL,12,Funusual frequency.
OL,13,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,131,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13012
SC,0012
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F130A1768740178
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                G12/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FStill, the move meant that many
OL,7,Fengineers would, understandably, only
OL,8,Fwant to install sets when a BBC Two
OL,9,Fsignal was available.B But the secret
OL,10,Fwas to make the most of the available
OL,11,Ftime ` not to make grim predictions
OL,12,Fabout increased fuel use like the
OL,13,Fwriter does.
OL,14,
OL,15,FAll a service engineer needed to do was
OL,16,Fbuy Radio Times to see when there'd be
OL,17,Fa BBC Two signal outside trade tests `
OL,18,Ffor instance because of midweek racing.
OL,19,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,131,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13013
SC,0013
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F130A1768740178
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                G13/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe countdown number on the test card
OL,7,Fwas introduced in 1976 to make it
OL,8,Feasier for engineers to use the limited
OL,9,Ftime ` not to tell viewers when
OL,10,Fprogrammes would resume.B
OL,11,
OL,12,FAll in all, it was a sensible economy
OL,13,Fcut. The sad thing is that the BBC's
OL,14,Ffinancial position and the state of the
OL,15,Fcountry made it necessary.
OL,16,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,131,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13014
SC,0014
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F130A1768740178
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                G14/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FIf took until 1983 to officially
OL,7,Freverse these cuts to BBC Two
OL,8,Ftransmission time. Shutdowns ended at
OL,9,Fthe same time as schools programmes
OL,10,Fmoved to Two.
OL,11,
OL,12,FIt's worth noting that things were
OL,13,Frelaxed slightly in 1980 when Ceefax
OL,14,FIn-Vision slots started ` usually in
OL,15,Fthe half hour up to 10.30am and 4pm.
OL,16,
OL,17,FIs any of this of relevance today or is
OL,18,Fit just anoraky nostalgia?
OL,19,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,131,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13015
SC,0015
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F130A1768740178
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                G15/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FEvery organisation needs to think about
OL,7,Fits energy bill and carbon footprint `
OL,8,Ffor both economic and environmental
OL,9,Freasons.
OL,10,
OL,11,FThe idea of a major channel being off
OL,12,Fthe air during the daytime is
OL,13,Funthinkable while multiplexing means
OL,14,Fthat the transmitter would still be on
OL,15,Fair even if an individual channel was
OL,16,Fshut.
OL,17,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,131,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13016
SC,0016
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F130A1768740178
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                G16/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FBut the Television article is a
OL,7,Freminder that it is possible to
OL,8,Foverstate the real challenges that
OL,9,Ftrying to save electricity can bring.
OL,10,
OL,11,FIt painted a worst case scenario and
OL,12,Fpresented it as inevitable.
OL,13,
OL,14,FWith sensible planning and foresight,
OL,15,Fmany businesses and some domestic
OL,16,Fcustomers todayB  could probably cut
OL,17,Ftheir power use and energy bills
OL,18,Fwithout too much hardship. Some already
OL,19,Fhave.
OL,20,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,131,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13017
SC,0017
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F130A1768740178
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                G17/17
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CLoss of BBC Two test card
OL,4,Ccauses trade "a great deal of trouble"
OL,5,
OL,6,FA growing proportion of the UK's
OL,7,Felectricity comes from renewables,
OL,8,Fnuclear powerB and "low carbon" sources
OL,9,Fsuch as biomass. Coal-fired power
OL,10,Fstations are a thing of the past.
OL,11,
OL,12,FModern lights and TVs use far less
OL,13,Felectricity than their 1970s
OL,14,Fequivalents.
OL,15,
OL,16,FBut the mindful use of power can help
OL,17,Fsome people and businesses cut their
OL,18,Felectricity bills without causing the
OL,19,Fhardship of simply switching something
OL,20,Foff.
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,131,120,200,300,0,100@
